diff --git a/docs/storage.md b/docs/storage.md
index 0de1bbf..5589889 100644
--- a/docs/storage.md
+++ b/docs/storage.md
@@ -60,6 +60,18 @@ Manual test plan: build and start the app, install it from Chrome, export a proj
 
 **Brand Projects, Storage** shows what DesignHub keeps on this device: the number and size of projects, version history, the icon cache and the offline caches, and the share of the space this browser allows. Only counts and sizes are read; no project content is shown or sent. **Clear the offline cache** deletes the `designhub-static-*` and `designhub-runtime-*` caches and nothing else (projects, settings and the share cache stay), and the studios you opened are kept again the next time you open them with a connection.
 
+## Keeping studios for offline use now
+
+A studio is kept for offline use the first time it is shown with a connection. For someone about to lose theirs, **Brand Projects, Storage, Keep studios for offline use** keeps studios ahead of time. It lists every studio with a checkbox and whether it is **Kept** or **Not kept**; **Select all not kept** ticks the rest, and **Keep selected** sends the service worker one message per studio, one after the other, with progress ("Keeping studio 2 of 5") and the size added so far.
+
+- **Nothing is downloaded until you press Keep selected.** Opening the panel, ticking a box or loading the page fetches nothing.
+- **A studio is kept whole or not at all.** Its files are stored first and its page last, and the page is stored only when every file is. If a download fails, that studio stays **Not kept**, the others are unaffected, and pressing **Keep selected** again fetches only what is missing.
+- **If something does not fit,** the panel says which studios are not ready and whether the device ran out of room (clear the offline cache or delete old versions, then try again) or a download failed (check the connection). Kept studios live in the `designhub-static-*` cache, which has no file limit, so the 300 file limit of the runtime cache never removes one and keeping studios never pushes out what the runtime cache holds.
+- **It needs the service worker to control the page.** That is the hosted site or a production build, a few seconds after the first visit and after a reload. In development, or before then, the panel says the worker is not running and the checkboxes are hidden.
+- **The sidebar marker follows.** A studio that is kept gets the "Available offline" marker straight away, with no reload, and **Clear the offline cache** takes the markers away again.
+
+For contributors: the page sends `{ type: "REMEMBER_ROUTE", pathname }` with a `MessagePort`, and the worker answers on it with `{ pathname, status, files, bytes, failed, full }` (`rememberRoute` in `scripts/service-worker-source.mjs`; the page side is `lib/pwa/keep-studios.ts`). A message without a port, which is what a page sends to say which studio it shows, still keeps the studio and gets no answer.
+
 ## Trimming old versions
 
 The Storage panel lists the projects that take the most room, with their history counted apart. **Delete versions older than** 30, 90 or 365 days shows how many versions that would remove, deletes them, and offers an Undo. The newest version of each project is always kept, and only the oldest part of a history is removed, so what is left is still a whole chain (see [Version history](#version-history)).
